tus (local run)\\n- Quick tests:\\n  - 10 passed, 3 deselected; coverage ~87% (above the 80% threshold).\\n- Benchmarks:\\n  - Logged a baseline throughput metric (stored in test output).\\n\\nOptional next steps\\n- Add coverage aggregation across matrix jobs and upload to a coverage service (Codecov/Coveralls) if desired.\\n- Store benchmark artifacts in a dashboard or GitHub Pages for trend tracking.\\n- Parameterize CI heavy run frequency or scale via repo variables.\\n- Enable pytest-xdist in CI for parallel test execution to cut runtime.\\n\\nIf you want, I can also add a codecov.yml and GitHub Action step to upload reports to Codecov.', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=True, action='message', security_risk=None), MessageAction(content='Please continue working on the task on whatever approach you think is suitable.\\nIf you think you have solved the task, please finish the interaction.\\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\\nIf you want to give up, run: <execute_bash> exit </execute_bash>.\\n', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=False, action='message', security_risk=None), RecallAction(recall_type='knowledge', query='Please continue working on the task on whatever approach you think is suitable.\\nIf you think you have solved the task, please finish the interaction.\\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\\nIf you want to give up, run: <execute_bash> exit </execute_bash>.\\n', thought='', action='recall'), CmdRunAction(command='cd /workspace/file-watcher-daemon && python run_tests.py', is_input=False, thought='', blocking=False, hidden=False, action='run', confirmation_state='confirmed', security_risk=None), CmdOutputObservation(content=\" test session starts \\nplatform linux -- Python 3.12.12, pytest-9.0.1, pluggy-1.6.0 -- /openhands/poetry/openhands-ai-5O4_aCHf-py3.12/bin/python\\ncachedir: .pytest_cache\\nbenchmark: 5.2.3 (defaults: timer=time.perf_counter disable_gc=False min_rounds=5 min_time=0.000005 max_time=1.0 calibration_pre